# External artifacts the jess oracles consume, pinned by digest.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (AFD-053 S2): every jess oracle defaulted to a path under
# .scratch/, which is gitignored. Nothing in the repo pinned what was supposed to be
# there, so 'against shipped gale-nano 0.7.0' and '10/10 digests verified' were
# asserted by FILENAME AND PROSE, not mechanically — and no one could reproduce a
# single result from a clean checkout. These digests make the claim checkable.
#
# Verified 2026-09-02: the five falcon components already in .scratch/v1341 are
# BYTE-IDENTICAL to relay's published falcon-v1.134.1 assets, so this pins what was
# actually used to produce AFD-046/-051/-052, not a lookalike.
#
# format:  <dest-path-under-.scratch>  <sha256>  <locator>
#
# The locator is what tools/deps/fetch.sh uses to RECONSTRUCT the byte from a clean
# checkout. Until 2026-09-04 these said only which release the artifact came from, which
# is not enough to fetch it — the upstream NAMES differ from the local ones. Two facts
# cost real time to establish and are recorded here so nobody re-derives them:
#
#   * The falcon stages are NOT standalone release assets. They live inside
#     falcon-components-v1.134.tar.gz and are named falcon-<stage>-v1.134.wasm upstream.
#     The mapping below was established BY DIGEST, not by guessing names.
#   * gale-nano is in NO gale release (checked v0.7.0/v0.7.1/v0.8.0 — the release carries
#     only the msgq/mutex/sem primitives). It is an OCI artifact at
#     ghcr.io/pulseengine/gale-nano:0.7.0, where its name is fused-gustos.component.wasm.
#
# grammar:
#   release:<owner>/<repo>@<tag>!<asset>[!<member-inside-tarball>]
#   oci:<ref>!<file-in-artifact>
#
# PLATFORM CAVEAT: fg60/synth is a Mach-O arm64 BINARY. Its digest is satisfiable only on
# aarch64-apple-darwin, so `platform=` records which host the pin is for and check.sh's
# green means nothing about a linux runner. Any CI use must verify against the release's
# own signed SHA256SUMS.txt instead. This is why the on-target oracles are not yet a CI
# gate (AFD-064 D4).

[falcon-v1.134.1]
